     "text": "Wilson Morgan and Gonzalez Medical Group\n\nRe: Kenneth Bryant (DOB 12/05/1959)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI am writing this letter to provide a comprehensive overview of Mr. Kenneth Bryant's medical history and current health status. letter is in response to your request for detailed information regarding Mr. Bryant's medical conditions and treatments.\n\nMr. Bryant has been under my care since 2022, and I have had several consultations with him regarding his various medical conditions.\n\nOn July 9, 2026, Mr. Bryant visited the clinic for an evaluation of his adrenal insufficiency. During this visit, his blood pressure was recorded at 129/75 mmHg, and his weight was 127 pounds. Mr. Bryant has been diagnosed with polycystic kidney disease, which is currently well controlled with eGFR of 93. Additionally, he has adrenal insufficiency, which is being managed with hydrocortisone 10 mg.\n\nOn September 13, 2025, Mr. Bryant returned for a follow-up on his polycystic kidney disease. His blood pressure was 134/74 mmHg, and his weight was 130 pounds. He continues to have well-controlled adrenal insufficiency.\n\nOn November 17, 2024, Mr. Bryant visited the clinic with symptoms of an upper respiratory infection (URI). His blood pressure at that time was 120/83 mmHg, and his weight was 126 pounds. He is otherwise doing well.\n\nOn January 22, 2024, Mr. Bryant came in for a routine check-up regarding his glaucoma. His blood pressure was 132/82 mmHg, and his weight was pounds. His polycystic kidney disease and adrenal insufficiency remain stable and well-managed.\n\nOn March 29, 2023, Mr. Bryant's cataracts were reviewed, with a blood pressure reading of 131/76 mmHg and a weight of 128 pounds. His polycystic kidney disease and adrenal insufficiency continue to be well-controlled.\n\nOn June 2, 2022, Mr. Bryant was seen for a rash. His blood pressure was 124/78 mmHg, and his weight was 118 pounds. His polycystic kidney disease and adrenal insufficiency remain stable.\n\nMr. Bryant has a history of smoking cigarettes, currently consuming about 2 per day since 1992. He also reports drinking approximately 3 alcoholic beverages per week.\n\nPlease note that the medications Mr. Bryant is currently taking include hydrocortisone 10 mg for adrenal insufficiency, latanoprost 0.005% and timolol ophthalmic 0.5% for glaucoma, and alendronate 70 mg for osteopenia.\n\nThis summary provides a thorough overview of Mr. Bryant's medical history and current health status. Should you require any further information, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Sally Barnett Medicine \n"
